2026-06-22 12:02:09,059 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 12:02:09,059 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To design the AI components and propose innovation strategies that meet the client's requirements, our approach at Faber IA will leverage our core capability in retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to provide an intelligent assistance tool. This tool will be grounded in the organization's own validated documents, including care protocols, HAS recommendations, internal procedures, applicable regulatory texts, and internal guides.

Our RAG approach allows for hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, template-guided drafting, and applicable rules recall during dossier handling. These capabilities can assist staff in drafting medical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters, thereby improving the quality of written outputs.

To facilitate access to information, our solution will provide retrieval trace, source citations, and every interaction logged for a posteriori audit, ensuring transparency and explainability. This aligns with the client's requirement for high-quality answers and the need to understand elements that led to an output.

In terms of reducing processing and documentation times, our assistant can surface relevant information at the point of need, assist in analyzing and handling dossiers, and suggest actions or verifications based on the dossier context and applicable rules. This is expected to decrease administrative and documentation work, increasing time available for patient care.

Our innovation strategy includes an iterative approach with steps such as corpus selection and curation with the client's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop. We will measure answer quality using a labeled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, and factual support.

We also prioritize data sovereignty and security, ensuring that all data is hosted exclusively within the European Union and protected appropriately. Our solution integrates with existing hospital information systems (SIH) and electronic patient records (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards like HL7 and FHIR.

Given our experience in similar use cases, such as the medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group, we are confident that our AI-powered intelligent assistance tool can meet the client's expectations by improving efficiency, quality of care, and staff satisfaction, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and data protection standards.
